# SolarEdge energy meters (Modbus meters wired to an inverter), SunSpec meter models 201-204.
# Meter 1 is at the default position; with Synergy inverters add 50 (2 units) or 70 (3 units) to every address.
# Only enabled meters can be read: if meters 1 and 3 are enabled they appear as meters 1 and 2.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=SolarEdge
@model=Energy meter (SunSpec 201-204)
@vendor_website=solaredge.com
@description=Export, import, production or consumption meters connected to a SolarEdge inverter, up to three, through SunSpec meter models. Line-to-line voltages are not supported by the SolarEdge meter
@source=SolarEdge, "SolarEdge Inverters - SunSpec Logging - Technical Note" v2.6 (December 2023), meter model register mapping; SunSpec Alliance information model definitions (github.com/sunspec/models), models 1 and 203
@protocol=tcp+rtu
@unit_id=1
@port=502
@baudrate=115200
@parity=N
@databits=8
@stopbits=1
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@sentinel_int16=-32768=Not implemented
@sentinel_uint16=0xFFFF=Not implemented
@sentinel_int32=-2147483648=Not implemented
@sentinel_uint32=0xFFFFFFFF=Not implemented

